return {
  summary = "Nuzlocke v3.0.3-beta: Gen 3 FireRed/LeafGreen/Hoenn challenges, player-controlled starter rerolls, expanded seeded randomiser, Run Journal and optional Untamed integration.",
  author = "bryanthaboi, Stone696 and Deluxe0111",
  contact = "https://github.com/Deluxe0111/nuzlocke",
  tags = { "ruleset", "hardcore", "quality-of-life", "ui" },
  differences = {
    changed = {
      "3.0.3-beta replaces automatic starter-trio balancing rolls with manual OFF/1/3/5/UNLIMITED reroll limits, persisted usage and rival-sync preservation; the optional companion Untamed/Modern Spawns enhancement ships separately.",
      "3.0.1-beta polishes and repackages the Gen 3 beta port: lean player ZIP without dev tests, curated release notes, improved GBA menu wrapping/area labels, verified CI and retained original credits.",
      "v3.0.0-BETA: First native FireRed/LeafGreen/Ruby/Sapphire/Emerald beta port, with all nine Advanced Rules categories, Gen 3 battle/catch/area/item/service adapters, Run Journal, terminal results posters, GBA menu, starting-resource setup and LOCK FOR RUN.",
      "v3.0.0-BETA: Seeded Gen 3 randomiser extends starter/wild/trainer/static/gift/Egg/item/shop/TM/learnset/evolution mappings; optional Untamed Advanced integration matches visible wandering spawns to battle/capture identity. Mod Support is read-only.",
      "v3.0.0-BETA: Hidden, test-save-audited Nuz Dev can restore only complete graveyard snapshots; ordinary Forgiveness revival remains unavailable. Wonderlocke was removed from the Gen 3 catalogue. Non-catch naming and third-party integrations still require ROM certification.",
      "v3.0.0-BETA credits: bryanthaboi (original Nuzlocke), Stone696 (legacy maintenance), masterwebx (original Shiny Pokemon lineage) and Deluxe0111 (Gen 3 port and integrations). See CREDITS.md for full attribution.",
      "Gen 3 PLAYSTYLES adds Shiny Nuzlocke: non-shiny wilds cannot be caught and never spend the route; eligible shinies still obey One Per Area, Failed Encounters and Dupes.",
      "v3.0.0-BETA introduces Generation 3 CORE, CLAUSES, LEVELS and RANDOMIZER, player notices, Graveyard/Dev tools and Untamed Advanced overworld wild compatibility; special chaining follows visible species.",
      "2.9.73 was the historical pre-v3 new-game QoL update: setup resources and native PC loadouts, deferred Poké Balls on capture unlock, and save.created resource handling. It does not include the subsequent completed v3 feature set.",
      "2.9.72 normalizes Gen-II item references, prevents legal Random Shop no-ops, exposes trainer boundary traces, and isolates shiny recoloring from shared engine ImageData; runtime retest required.",
      "2.9.71 repairs Gen-I Random Field Items by moving visible pickup composition to the public world.talk hook, adds focused hook/pipeline diagnostics, and preserves native pickup behavior; runtime retest is required.",
      "2.9.70 advances the Gen1Recomp source-review baseline to 0.2.41 and fixes normalized input-profile fallback metadata so reported profile identity matches resolved behavior; no gameplay or schema contract changes.",
      "2.9.69 fixes conditional presentation/gameplay authority semantics and removes a stale UI API version pin from the input-contract Release Safety check; no gameplay or schema contracts change.",
      "2.9.68 fixes the Gen-II Nuzlocke utility-screen draw crash caused by a missing Typography.centerX helper and adds a Release Safety consumer/definition guard; gameplay and public compatibility contracts are otherwise unchanged.",
      "2.9.67 fixes the Dev Report runtime crash caused by an unresolved compatPublicCopy global by restoring explicit dependency injection from main.lua into dev_diagnostics.lua and adding a Release Safety split-safety guard; gameplay and public contracts are unchanged.",
      "2.9.66 adds UI presentation-ownership contract v1 (UI API 8), explicitly targets HGSS Visual Overhaul 1.0.2 for Yellow presentation coexistence, and hardens the Gen-I Random Trainer constructor wrapper contract for order-independent chaining with presentation mods without changing gameplay authority.",
      "2.9.65 adds a semantic Nuzlocke UI input contract that distinguishes repeat-safe navigation/value stepping from edge-only activation/back and destructive confirmation; the contract is presentation-only and does not intercept engine or external-mod input.",
      "2.9.64 advances the Gen1Recomp source/documentation compatibility audit through 0.2.39 and explicitly yields PresentSync/PresentProbe, VSync, FrameCap, and FixedStep presentation pacing to the engine; only read-only PresentSync diagnostics are added and no runtime certification is promoted.",
      "2.9.56 adds evolution_policy.lua as the dedicated owner for Evolution Limits and Trade Evolution QoL over the shared evolution.check seam; Randomizer evolution mappings, UI/config, identity/provenance, and acquisition policy remain with their existing owners; consolidation is paused after this build by user direction.",
      "2.9.55 adds item_policy.lua as the dedicated owner for item-use legality, denial presentation, and ItemEffects/field-action guard installation while leaving economy policy and battle orchestration with their existing owners; the protected package contract advances to 36 files / 26 Lua modules plus mod.card.",
      "2.9.53 adds encounter_tracker.lua as the dedicated owner for area catalogs, encounter projection, tracker persistence, and reconstruction while consuming pokemon_identity.lua for identity/provenance facts; public contracts and runtime evidence are unchanged.",
      "2.9.44 continues conservative modularization by moving pure read-only save-schema descriptor describe/structural-audit logic into rule_catalog.lua; live schema, migration, transaction, and persistence ownership remain in main.lua and public behavior is unchanged.",
      "2.9.41 resumes conservative modularization by moving pure rule-value coercion into rule_catalog.lua with a live definition-index dependency and parity-certified behavior; gameplay, persistence, and public APIs are unchanged.",
      "2.9.40 audits Release Safety toward semantic checks and classifies compatibility evidence without changing gameplay, provider ownership, persistence, or public API versions.",
      "2.9.38 adds a generated read-only save-key/reference consumer index with bounded fail-open diagnostics; persistence behavior, schema, gameplay policy, and runtime evidence are unchanged.",
      "2.9.37 adds semantic catch-denial disposition reconciliation and numeric enum/range completeness certification without changing gameplay policy or runtime evidence.",
      "2.9.30 repairs Colorlocke with a complete Gen-I/II canonical Pokedex-search color fallback and semantic Release Safety coverage; custom unknown species still fail open and presentation palettes never determine legality.",
      "2.9.28 adds Blackjack Corner 0.8.2 as a high-overlap source-reviewed compatibility target and adds experimental semantic battle-roster/activity-state observation APIs for cooperative mods; no gameplay rule or save-schema change.",
      "2.9.26 adds source-reviewed compatibility targets for Double Battles 0.6.1 and Free Fly 1.8.0 while preserving external mechanic ownership and requiring combined runtime certification.",
      "2.9.25 adds Colorlocke and Alphabetlocke as composable prospective acquisition restrictions with deterministic RANDOM and explicit CHOOSE modes; existing Pokemon/evolutions remain untouched and unknown custom metadata fails open.",
      "2.9.24 formalizes permanent upstream attribution for bryanthaboi, masterwebx, and Stone696 across package documentation and project governance; no gameplay behavior changes.",
      "2.9.23 advances Gen1Recomp source/documentation/launcher compatibility review through 0.2.38, confirming the existing Nuzlocke manifest fits current launcher update/version/status metadata without changing gameplay ownership or save contracts.",
      "2.9.1 audits party-stack ownership: Modern Party UI remains presentation-only, native controller routing is preserved, and Gen-II party routing stays protected.",
      "2.8.98 advances the Gen1Recomp source/documentation compatibility baseline to 0.2.36 while preserving engine ONLINE policy and pending runtime certification.",
      "2.8.97 adds read-only Gen-II Random Field Item decision/script-projection diagnostics and static native-builder/wrapper auditing while preserving 2.8.88 method-specific ownership and mappings.",
      "2.8.89 adds read-only Gen-II Random Trainer pipeline diagnostics and static hook/native-constructor auditing while preserving the existing randomization algorithm pending exact runtime reproduction.",
      "2.8.88 separates TM contents from TM pickup-location randomization, adds a dedicated deterministic TM-location option, and enforces source/method-specific external Randomizer ownership at the actual field-item execution seam so visible, hidden, TM-location, and TM-content methods can coexist without double transformation.",
      "2.8.87 refreshes external Randomizer coexistence against Pokemon Gen 1 Randomizer 0.46.4, Gen 2 Randomizer+ published 2.9.0, and Item Randomizer 1.1.1; active overlapping trainer/evolution/shop/field-item/TM subsystems now delegate narrowly to avoid double randomization, while installation alone remains non-owning.",
      "2.8.83 completes the Shiny-ecosystem voxel target sweep by adding Dramatic Shape Voxel Mod 1.0.6 as an explicit Gen-I presentation coexistence target without creating a manifest dependency; existing PotatoVoxel, PokéPC, Followers EX, Wilds, Shiny and Nuzlocke-specific targets remain intact.",
      "2.8.81 fixes stored-state DEV diagnostics accounting so the Phase-H economy regression audit is counted as present when its audit function exists and runs; gameplay behavior and public APIs are unchanged.",
      "2.8.80 fixes failed-area F. TOKEN spend confirmation so repeated directional input keeps the intended YES/NO selection instead of flipping it; public APIs and save schema are unchanged.",
      "2.8.79 reconciles player-facing documentation, support/confidence wording, public contracts, and compatibility boundaries without changing gameplay behavior or public API versions.",
      "2.8.78 audits Gen1Recomp 0.2.30-0.2.33, corrects upstream Save Format profile metadata, revalidates protected Gen II and Crystal shiny-flash seams, and documents ONLINE-arena and future hook opportunities without claiming new runtime certification.",
      "2.8.77 hardens migration copy isolation, Compatibility API runtime-environment semantics, provider bundle atomicity, and Gen2 Randomizer Hook Health diagnostics.",
      "2.8.76 fixes three confirmed correctness issues: R/B/Y Ball item-policy exceptions now fail closed and refund safely, F. Token recovery only treats FAILED encounter states as failed projections, and World Building certification accounts for all six exact editions.",
      "2.8.75 fixes Run History death-event shiny evidence so an explicit false value is preserved instead of falling through to live Pokemon shiny detection, and adds a focused regression self-test.",
      "2.8.74 fixes deterministic gift fallback for the Route 4 Magikarp and adds a catalog-driven consistency self-test so all version-neutral Gen-I gifts must remain synchronized with fallback classification.",
      "2.8.73 hardens durable gameplay transactions against same-ID/same-kind payload collisions, makes external item-policy evaluator exceptions fail closed instead of authorizing item use, and repairs the transaction self-test future-version case without changing gameplay features or public contracts.",
      "2.8.72 gives Difficulty confirmation a native visible cursor, replaces opaque/percent-glyph-dependent in-game Difficulty copy with concise plain-language exact examples, makes Difficulty Review details scrollable, adds exact Silver and Crystal profile catalogs, and makes full profile mechanics documentation a release-safety requirement.",
      "2.8.71 fixes the Discord-reported Gen1/Yellow Difficulty Review crash caused by an out-of-scope wrapPixelText call, adds R/B/Y Profile Slot/Save/Load presentation parity with visible state/result feedback, and adds a Release Safety numeric-rule registry bounds audit.",
      "2.8.70 fixes three Run History v2 correctness regressions: run.abandoned now has a durable summary/backfill and reconstructed flag, partial-detail coverage is generalized across all summarized event kinds (including live pruning/existing v2 roots), and stored-state diagnostics now validate against the current Run History storage version instead of stale literal v1.",
      "2.8.69 consolidates the full translation compatibility registry, normalizes primary/alternate/overlay/legacy target roles, fixes missing Finnish optional ordering, and records reviewed placeholders/forks/tooling/engine-fork repositories outside runtime companion detection.",
      "2.8.68 adds spanish_translation 0.1.0 as a separate alternate Red-only Spanish target, preserving traduccion_es as the primary Spanish target and recording its versaovermelha fork lineage, battle UI override, and confirmed-loaded replacement scripts.",
      "2.8.67 promotes finnish 0.1.0 from upstream-unverified to the current conservative Red-only Finnish target, recording its fixed-cell extended-Latin glyphs, invasive presentation overrides, confirmed-loaded replacement scripts, and focused localization certification seams.",
      "2.8.66 adds translation-nl 0.0.2 as the current Dutch Red/Blue target, recording its English fallback/ASCII-folding model and confirmed runtime loading of mutation-capable replacement handlers under the generalized replacement-script policy.",
      "2.8.65 adds zh_cn 0.3.1 as the primary Simplified Chinese Red/Blue/Yellow target and formalizes a generalized narrow/compositional translation-presentation wrapper contract for Strings/Font/UI engine-gap overlays.",
      "2.8.64 adds recomp-polish 1.0.0 as the current conservative Red-only Polish target, with fixed-cell extended-Latin/fallback metadata and replacement-script mutation review marked as present but runtime loading unconfirmed.",
      "2.8.63 adds primary Italian translation-it 0.6.0 and alternate recomp-italian 0.1.0 targets, plus a generalized replacement-map-script mutation compatibility contract so translated interaction scripts cannot silently bypass Nuzlocke semantic policy.",
      "2.8.62 adds session-only manual localization runtime-certification tooling to Dev Report, keyed to exact edition + detected translation IDs/versions/language state, with a 10-surface checklist and compact certification snapshot.",
      "2.8.61 removes remaining player-facing byte-length/byte-slice assumptions found by the Japanese/CJK audit, sharing glyph helpers across split modules, hardening Pokegear/recovery/dev/status surfaces, and adding their stable translation sources.",
      "2.8.60 adds explicit Japanese Red/Blue compatibility for translation-ja-hrkt 0.4.2 and hardens/document the existing UTF-8/glyph-span layout boundary for CJK text.",
      "2.8.59 adds the formal translation compatibility matrix and expands Translation API 2 source discovery across Forgiveness/F. TOKEN UI, Battle Clause denials, common status/compatibility labels, and selected runtime messages.",
      "2.8.58 adds explicit compatibility for generated Translation French 0.8.0 (translation-fr) across all six supported editions and Traduction FR etendue 0.2.0 as a separate optional gap-filling overlay, with language-neutral Release Safety guards.",
      "2.8.57 adds explicit compatibility for Traduccion Espanola 0.1.0 (traduccion_es), including optional load ordering, Red/Blue cartridge-layer scope documentation, partial-without-EUR-dump behavior, and Release Safety against Spanish gameplay-literal matching.",
      "2.8.56 hardens Nuzlocke-owned UI for long/variable-width translated text, expands Translation API 2 discovery across the full World Building flavor catalog and Randomizer status/value labels, and localizes dynamic Randomizer/type-lock inserted values.",
      "2.8.55 expands the Translation API 2 source catalog with high-value Nuzlocke UI/status/tracker/world-summary strings and adds read-only localization lifecycle/fallback diagnostics to Dev System Health and DEV REPORT.",
      "2.8.54 adds explicit Translation German Universal 0.2.0 compatibility, advances nuzlocke_translation API 1→2 with installed-vs-active language lifecycle diagnostics, and protects canonical encounter-area identity from localized display names.",
      "2.8.53 fixes compatibility ownership so disabled/inactive providers cannot be selected, canonicalizes API-35 capability snapshots, keys GameplayTransactions journals/recovery to TX.api, and preserves explicit Run History critical=false evidence.",
      "2.8.52 fixes DEV REPORT > SHINY so unset Shiny Colors and Shiny Intro settings report their authoritative default ON state, matching Rule Catalog and runtime behavior.",
      "2.8.51 fixes false-value preservation in schema migration shadow/apply/rollback state and the durable save.set_exact transaction coordinator, restoring exact absent/false/true/value semantics across interruption recovery.",
      "2.8.50 adds explicit Brazilian translation compatibility for current VersaoVermelha 0.2.5 while retaining legacy gen1_pt-br, generalizes translation presentation diagnostics, and removes the Forgiveness shop filter's English display-label dependency.",
      "2.8.49 adds Run History v2 achievement-evidence aggregates: lifetime counters/dimensions survive the bounded event journal, rule changes are tracked for future run-integrity achievements, and failed encounters are now journaled. Save Schema remains 5.",
      "2.8.48 advances Compatibility API 34→35 to formally version semantic provider/capability status + compatibility snapshots, and source-audits Gen1Recomp 0.2.28/0.2.29. Save Schema remains 5; engine minimum remains >=0.2.24 <2.0.0.",
      "2.8.48 advances Compatibility API 34 -> 35 to formally version semantic provider/capability status introspection, and source-audits Gen1Recomp 0.2.28/0.2.29 while retaining the >=0.2.24 engine floor and Save Schema 5.",
      "2.8.47 is a documentation/release reconciliation pass: current README, User Guide, API contract, engine/support status, Randomizer scope, shiny ownership, compatibility wording, and selected rule descriptions are synchronized to the shipped implementation. Gameplay behavior is unchanged.",
      "2.8.46 completes the current Dev Mode backlog with read-only RULE CONFIG consistency, SAVE/RUN identity health, and bounded session-only OWNER HISTORY diagnostics.",
      "2.8.45 adds severity-aware repetition coalescing to bounded Dev breadcrumbs/decision traces and a read-only PERFORMANCE page backed by cheap in-memory Dev-only counters for selected Randomizer builders.",
      "2.8.44 adds read-only Dev Mode SHINY and RANDOM REPRO pages. Shiny diagnostics expose ownership/configured presentation/materialized identity without rolling; Randomizer reproducibility consumes the existing zero-RNG persisted run-contract/source-map report.",
      "2.8.43 adds read-only Dev Mode TRANSACTIONS and HOOK DRIFT pages. Transaction Health summarizes the durable gameplay journal/receipts and fail-closed recovery policy; Hook Drift reports wrapper interposition/replacement without reclaiming ownership.",
      "2.8.42 adds a read-only Dev Mode BUG REPORT snapshot that aggregates build/engine/edition, save/run identity, System Health, provider ownership, current encounter provenance, recent decisions, warnings/errors, and recent breadcrumbs without invoking rules, RNG, self-tests, or repair paths.",
      "2.8.41 upgrades diagnostics-only Dev Mode with System Health, provider ownership detail, live encounter provenance, and a bounded semantic rule-decision trace for core catch/item/economy denials.",
      "2.8.40 expands Release Safety/static regression coverage without gameplay changes: battle/party ownership, shiny single-owner boundaries, transaction journaling, battle.started event shapes, and structural Randomizer performance contracts are now promotion-gated.",
      "2.8.38 begins localization hardening without gameplay changes: Battle Clause denials, Forgiveness actions, Classic NUZ STATUS / Run History templates, and Legacy Recovery fallbacks now use Gen1Recomp Strings, with targeted Release Safety coverage.",
      "2.8.37 promotes the corrected 2.8.36 line to a full release after Red runtime PASS for standalone ALWAYS-shiny generation, species recoloring, and shiny intro presentation; the tested shiny code path is unchanged.",
      "2.8.36 adds full provider-absent shiny presentation through current Gen1Recomp sprite/icon/overlay seams, with Shiny Colors and Shiny Intro controls and immediate full stand-down when a compatible external shiny provider owns the edition.",
      "2.8.35 clarifies the adjacent shiny controls without changing mechanics: Shiny Clause controls catch exceptions only, while Shiny Rate controls rarity only; summaries and safety checks preserve the distinction.",
      "2.8.34 adds explicit SHINY_POKEMON provider compatibility plus a built-in Shiny Rate fallback: Gen-I external providers own roll/presentation when healthy, provider-absent Gen I gains identity/rate semantics without DV/stat rewrites, and Gen II composes through the public shiny.roll seam.",
      "2.8.33 adds explicit/generalized PotatoVoxel renderer compatibility: presentation ownership stays with the voxel mod while Nuzlocke keeps gameplay/rule authority, MOD COMPAT reports the provider, and Release Safety blocks Nuzlocke from seizing render.compose, Gen2BattleState, or native BattleState draw methods.",
      "2.8.32 adds explicit live type-chart compatibility while preserving the Silver-tested Gen-2 Random Starter selection/award path and fixes the two remaining Elm text surfaces: confirmation no longer falls back to ellipsis, and the native received announcement names the randomized starter instead of the vanilla ball species.",
      "2.8.29 makes Battle Menu UI Gen-1-only at hook-registration time and replaces the Gen-2 custom battle-rule pager phase with the native BattleState refusal path; Wilds 2.2.0 compatibility observability is ported from the quarantined 2.8.28 comparison.",
      "2.8.27 removes all Nuzlocke method wrappers from Gen-2 PartyMenu so battle cancellation and direct item targeting remain native.",
      "2.8.03 retries Gen-2 party-item and field-poison wipe timing at earlier authoritative seams, and audits/restores the complete Gen-2 Randomizer parent/child configuration surface.",
      "2.8.01 hotfix restores Gen-2 Trainer Randomizer Setup/Rules options and independently detects last-usable-party field-poison wipes so they cannot silently continue.",
      "2.8.00 full release moves Gen-2 simple party-consumable commit ownership to the Pack seam using the authoritative live save-party slot and native ItemEffects, and slightly slows the five-stage Setup/Rules navigation ramp.",
      "2.7.106 repairs the shared Gen-2 post-selection consumable seam for healing/status/revive items, vitamins, and Rare Candy using native ItemEffects, and retunes held Setup/Rules navigation to five-stage acceleration.",
      "2.7.105 fixes the confirmed Gen-2 party-item chooser-mode regression so USE-on-Pokemon screens stay direct choosers, and adds held UP/DOWN auto-repeat to Nuzlocke Setup/Rules while preserving SELECT section jumps.",
      "2.7.104 preserves the runtime-PASS TOOLS profile controls, retires the unsuccessful direct Gen-2 Pack routing experiment, and rematerializes tracked randomized Elm starters against Gen1Recomp's native Gen-2 Mon record contract before party-item use.",
      "2.7.103 routes native Gen-2 party consumables directly to Game2 party-item ownership after Nuzlocke legality checks, restores distinct Profile Slot/Save/Load semantics, and returns World Building defaults to T3 in every game.",
      "2.7.101 repairs Gen-2 Center Heal and Shop Restrictions visibility, adds in-run TOOLS profile save/load plus Encounter Assignment, hardens Crystal DST skip, and advances the Gen1Recomp audit through 0.2.25 while preserving Random Starter behavior.",
      "2.7.95 preserves the runtime-PASS 2.7.94 Random Starter repair while fixing Gen-2 Encounter Tracker MAP ordering/filtering, Setup monochrome presentation, MOD COMPAT geometry/blinking navigation, and the optional Battle Menu UI pixel-box layout.",
      "2.7.94 repairs the runtime-bisected Random Starter regression introduced in 2.7.45 by restoring starter-specific Species Pool isolation, while preserving Species Pool for encounter/trainer/evolution randomizers and all later Randomizer hardening.",
      "2.7.93 fails Crystal starter-ball presentation open to the native animated portrait/cry path while preserving the shared GIVEPOKE transaction, and repairs stale DEV REPORT Randomizer validation expectations.",
      "2.7.84 intentionally enables Pokemon Crystal as ALPHA support after the Gen1Recomp 0.2.24-era compatibility/documentation audit; shared Gen-2 routing is reused, Crystal receives independent edition identity/evidence, and compatibility tripwires are updated for six editions.",
      "2.7.83 implements the planned Rules/Setup UI batch: direct loadout and Difficulty selection, compact rule navigation, manual Gen-2 time control, and explicit deferred Starting Ball wording.",
      "2.7.73 reconstructs from exact 2.7.72 and repairs Late Runtime dependency ordering without changing rule semantics.",
      "2.7.70 continues the exact-game rule audit: Yellow hides native Trio Typing, encounter-slot modifiers depend on One Per Area, and Type Locke shows only active non-draft lanes; dormant choices remain behaviorally inert.",
      "2.7.64 adds MOD COMPAT owner cycling for contract-backed capabilities, with AUTO/native/provider choices and pre-commit warnings for gameplay-impacting ownership changes.",
      "2.7.63 repairs Gold/Silver Encounter Tracker MAP ordering and adds a confirmation warning before Difficulty changes that alter trainer-rule semantics.",
      "2.7.62 repairs Gold/Silver No Center Heal and No Mom Heal at the native Gen II HealParty special seam and adds a Release Safety cross-generation semantic-seam audit.",
      "2.7.60 hardens additional presentation/source audits so cosmetic/source drift remains promotion-blocking without bricking startup, while preserving gameplay-critical fail-fast guards.",
      "2.7.59 repairs the stale World Building presentation-catalog checksum that could abort startup and moves presentation-only catalog drift to diagnostics/Release Safety instead of boot failure.",
      "2.7.58 extends shared row/notice primitives across Gen I/Gen II, migrates F. TOKEN and Dev Tools action presentation, and adds optional compatibility ordering for variable-width kerning.",
      "2.7.57 makes Nuzlocke typography provider-neutral, removes the internal kerning shim, adds live font-metric measurement/fitting/wrapping, semantic rows/statuses/notices, and typography stress fixtures.",
      "2.7.56 adds explicit logical-surface policies, real wide-capable Gen I Rules/Setup and Tracker composition, centered child-flow continuity, and the Dev-only UI Gallery.",
      "2.7.55 adds the shared Nuzlocke-owned UI architecture foundation for Rules/Setup and Encounter Tracker while preserving gameplay authority and protected native/external surfaces.",
      "2.7.39 advances Evolution Randomizer Phase G through split-evolution handling and explicit evolution-method/Gen2 trigger preservation.",
      "2.7.35 advances Trainer Randomizer Phase F through team diversity, optional type cohesion, and rival-starter synchronization.",
      "2.7.34 advances Trainer Randomizer Phase F through legality, evolutionary-stage scaling, and BST/power balancing while preserving authored trainer levels.",
      "2.7.32 adds Gold long-help above/below orientation plus exact scroll-position feedback and establishes one shared rule-feedback language contract.",
      "2.7.31 makes Gold long-help paging discoverable with SEL:MORE/SEL:TOP and aligns Select scrolling with the native four-line help renderer.",
